      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Azimuthal quantum number ℓ, jise angular momentum quantum number bhi kehte hain, har n ke liye 0 se (n − 1) tak whole number qeematein le sakta hai. Yeh orbital ki shape (shakal) batata hai. ℓ ki qeematein n par depend karti hain: n = 1 ho to sirf ℓ = 0; n = 2 ho to ℓ = 0 aur 1; n = 3 ho to 0, 1 aur 2; aur n = 4 ho to 0, 1, 2 aur 3. ℓ ki qeematon ko letters s, p, d aur f se likhte hain, jo sharp, principal, diffused aur fundamental ke liye hain. Yeh spectral lines ki kuch khoobiyan batane wale purane spectral terms hain."
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "correction",
            "title": "Kitab ki ghalti",
            "text": "Kitab n = 2 ke liye ℓ ki qeematein ‘0 aur ℓ’ likhti hai. Sahi: 0 aur 1."
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "definition",
            "title": "Subshell",
            "text": "Jin orbitals ke n aur ℓ dono ek jaise hon, un ke set ko subshell kehte hain."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Kisi subshell ke zyada se zyada electrons formula 2(2ℓ + 1) se nikalte hain, jaisa Table 2.3 mein hai."
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "Table 2.3 Orbitals ki shapes",
            "header": [
              "ℓ ki qeemat",
              "0",
              "1",
              "2",
              "3"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Orbital ka naam",
                "s",
